<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Semion Morozov   unloading   maize grits     2,950     Europe</p>
<p>Bobaibo	    17/02	 bran		2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Nazly Poyrez     18/02	 barley	   15,487     U.S.</p>
<p>Lake Champlain   19/02	 barley	   24,500     U.S.</p>
<p>Sormovky 8	 20/02	 barley	    2,988     Europe</p>
<p>Kapitan Baglay   21/02	 fish meal	 5,000     Peru</p>
<p>Semion Rudnov    25/02	 maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Salechard	  25/02	 feed wheat	3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Nikolay Lebedev  28/02	 maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Sarha		01/03	 corn, sorghum, 63,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	01/03	 n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
